---
description: Hearth stack conventions — Python (FastAPI) + React (Vite/TS) + nginx, Docker Compose dev loop
alwaysApply: true
---

## Languages and runtimes

- **Python 3.12** for hub gateway, plugin loader, Spark message bus, and most plugin backends.
  - Async-first (FastAPI, `asyncio`, `httpx`).
  - Type hints everywhere; `mypy --strict` in CI.
  - Lint/format: `ruff` (lint + format) — no `black` / `isort` overlap.
  - Tests: `pytest` + `pytest-asyncio`. One behavior per test, no shared mutable fixtures unless documented.
- **C++20** is reserved for performance-critical background services (media transcode, CV, on-device ML). Not required for MVP. When introduced, use CMake + `clang-format` (LLVM style) and document in a per-component README.
- **TypeScript 5.x** + **React 18** for all UIs. Vite for dev/build, **Vite-PWA** for manifest + service worker. ESLint + Prettier (project-wide config from Mantle). The hub UI is a PWA by default; plugins inherit Mantle's shell and do not register their own service workers in MVP.
- **Bash** allowed only for thin invocation wrappers (`./develop`, container entrypoints). Anything with branching belongs in Python.

## Build / test / lint

- All development commands run inside Docker Compose (or the configured Dev Container) before host execution. Use `./develop <cmd>` wrappers; document host-only exceptions in the ticket diary.
- Unit tests are required for new behavior and bug fixes. Skip only for docs-only changes and pure scaffolding.

## Project layout (target)

```
apps/
  hub/                # FR-0001 hub app (Python backend + React UI)
    api/              # FastAPI app (gateway, plugin registry, settings)
    web/              # React + Vite UI (uses Mantle)
  <plugin-slug>/      # Future plugin apps (one folder each, optional submodule)
plugins.d/            # Discovered plugin manifest snapshots (runtime data, gitignored)
deploy/
  compose/            # Docker Compose for dev + Pi/Mac mini deploy
  caddy/              # Caddyfile templates and route generators (default proxy)
  nginx/              # nginx alternative (parity templates)
  systemd/            # systemd unit templates for bare-metal install
  install.sh          # one-shot Pi/Mac mini installer
docs/                 # Authoritative design docs (see docs/design/)
tasks/                # Process state (see docs/ai-context.md)
.skeleton/            # Process template submodule
```

## Naming

- Plugin slugs: `kebab-case`, ASCII, ≤ 32 chars (e.g. `groceries`, `idea-catcher`).
- Python modules: `snake_case`. React components: `PascalCase`. CSS classes: Tailwind utility-first; reusable patterns live in Mantle.
- Routes: hub at `/`; each plugin at `/<slug>/...` (proxied by Caddy by default; nginx alternative supported).

## Cross-cutting rules

- **Mantle is the only place** for shared UI primitives. Plugins **must not** ship duplicate theme/nav code; pull from Mantle (Kindling submodule). The PWA manifest + service worker live in Mantle; plugins do not register their own SW in MVP.
- **Spark is the only sanctioned channel** for app-to-app traffic. Plugins **must not** call each other's proxy routes directly.
- **Tinder manifests are validated at load**. A plugin without a valid manifest is registered but disabled with the validation error visible in the dashboard.
- **Secrets** (relay keys, OAuth client secrets, cloud-storage tokens) live in `var/hearth/secrets/` (mode 0600, gitignored). `.env*` files are not committed; only `.env.example` placeholders.

## Hearth CLI parity (production operator surface)

- **Scope:** The **`hearth`** admin CLI and per-plugin **`plugin`** CLI (see **`FR-0003`**, design contract: [Docker profile (Pi)](../../docs/design/deployment.md#docker-profile-pi) in **`docs/design/deployment.md`**) are the **default operator control plane** for Compose-based installs on Pi-class hosts.
- **Rule:** When you add or change an **operator-facing** platform capability (stack lifecycle, plugin lifecycle, backup/restore, TLS/CA export, updates, diagnostics), you **must** either:
  - expose it through **`hearth`** / **`plugin`** in the same change series, **or**
  - add an explicit **follow-up ticket** on the active **`FR-NNNN`** (or a new **`FR-NNNN`**) titled so `identify-frontier` can schedule CLI parity, and note the gap in the feature diary.
- **UI follow-up:** Web admin surfaces should wrap the same contracts later; do not treat “UI-only” as done for operations that operators must perform over SSH.

## Tie-back to design

- Module-level docstrings reference `docs/design/...` where the behavior is specified.
- Use the traceability prefix `@HRT-<AREA>-<NUMBER>` (areas in `docs/design/documentation-style.md`).
